              ----------------------------------------
               Guidelines for iist.cls LaTeX Template 
              ----------------------------------------
              https://github.com/4sarathbabu/IISTThesis


The 'iist.cls' LaTeX template enables students to prepare
professional-quality reports and theses with minimal effort, while
adhering to the formatting requirements of IIST.


1. How to Start?
----------------

The template is implemented through the LaTeX class file 'iist.cls',
which is included in this repository. The main document to be compiled
is 'doct.tex'. The first line of doct.tex specifies the document class
and its options, which determine the degree program and document type
(e.g., internship report, project report, thesis, or synopsis). The
supported document class configurations are listed below.

  B.Tech Internship: \documentclass[btech,internship,twoside]{iist} 
  B.Tech Project: \documentclass[btech,project,twoside]{iist}    
  M.Tech Thesis: \documentclass[mtech,thesis,twoside]{iist}     
  M.S Thesis: \documentclass[ms,thesis,twoside]{iist}        
  PhD Thesis: \documentclass[phd,thesis,twoside]{iist}       
  PhD Synopsis: \documentclass[phd,synopsis,twoside]{iist}     

Notes:

 (a) To generate a single-sided document, remove the 'twoside' option
     from the '\documentclass' declaration.

 (b) The template uses Computer Modern as the default font. To use
     Times New Roman-style fonts instead, add the following line
     immediately after the '\documentclass' declaration in doct.tex:

     \usepackage{times}


2. Specifying Credentials of the Report/Thesis
----------------------------------------------

The template simplifies document preparation by requiring report or
thesis information to be specified only once in 'doct.tex'. This
information is automatically propagated to the relevant front-matter
pages, including the Title Page, Certificate, Declaration, and
Acknowledgements. The available metadata commands are listed below:

  Document Title: \title{}
  Author: \author{}
  Author ID: \studentid{}
  Project/Thesis Advisor: \advisor{}
  Specialization: \specialization{}
  Department: \department{}
  Date: \date{}  


3. Creating Initial Pages of the Report/Thesis
----------------------------------------------

The front-matter pages, including the Title Page, Certificate,
Declaration, Dedication, and Acknowledgements, are generated
automatically using the document information provided in
'doct.tex'. To customize the content of any of these pages, edit the
corresponding TeX source file listed below.

  Certificate: 'certificate.tex'
  Declaration: 'declaration.tex'
  Dedication: 'dedication.tex'
  Acknowledgements: 'acknowledgements.tex'
  Abstract: 'abstract.tex'
  Abbreviations: 'abbreviations.tex'
  Nomenclature: 'nomenclature.tex'
  Publications: 'publications.tex'

The Table of Contents, List of Figures, List of Tables, and List of
Algorithms are automatically generated and updated based on the
content of the report or thesis.

Note: A Ph.D. synopsis typically does not require certain front-matter
pages. Therefore, you may comment out the following commands in
'doct.tex': \makecertificate, \makedeclaration, \makededication,
\makeacknowledgements, \makelistoffigures, \makelistoftables, and
\makelistofalgorithms in 'doct.tex'. Please DO NOT comment the line
\makechaptersettings.


4. Addition of Chapters, Appendices, and List of Publications
-------------------------------------------------------------

It is recommended to organize each chapter in a separate TeX source
file (e.g., 'chapter1.tex', 'chapter2.tex', and
'chapter3.tex'). Individual chapters can then be included in
'doct.tex' using the '\input' command:

			\input{chapter1}

Appendices may be organized similarly, with each appendix maintained
in a separate file. For example, this template includes
'appendixA.tex' and 'appendixB.tex' for Appendix A and Appendix B,
respectively. The list of publications can also be maintained as a
separate chapter in 'publications.tex'.

For a Ph.D. synopsis, which typically does not contain chapters, the
entire content may be placed in 'chapter1.tex' and included in
'doct.tex' using \input{chapter1}. In this case, remove the line
'\chapter{...}' command from 'chapter1.tex'.


5. Writing Theorems, Proofs, Lemmas, Definitions, Remarks,
-----------------------------------------------------------
Assumptions, and Propositions
------------------------------

The template defines the following mathematical and theorem-like
environments:

    Theorem     :    \begin{theorem} ... \end{theorem}
    Proof       :    \begin{proof} ... \end{proof}             
    Lemma       :    \begin{lemma} ... \end{lemma}
    Corollary	:    \begin{corollary} ... \end{corollary}
    Proposition :    \begin{proposition} ... \end{proposition}
    Conjecture	:    \begin{conjecture} ... \end{conjecture}
    Definition  :    \begin{definition} ... \end{definition}
    Condition	:    \begin{condition} ... \end{condition}
    Assumption  :    \begin{assumption} ... \end{assumption}
    Example	:    \begin{example} ... \end{example}
    Problem	:    \begin{problem} ... \end{problem}
    Remark     	:    \begin{remark} ... \end{remark}
    Claim	:    \begin{claim}  ... \end{claim}
    Note	:    \begin{note} ... \end{note}


6. Addition of Bibliography
---------------------------

The template supports bibliography management through BibTeX. Citation
entries should be stored in 'doct.bib', and the bibliography can be
included in 'doct.tex' using the following commands:

			\bibliographystyle{IEEEtran}
			\bibliography{doct}

By default, the template uses the IEEE bibliography style
(IEEEtran). This can be changed to any supported BibTeX style,
including unsrt, plain, and apa.


7. Building the LaTeX Source
----------------------------

If the tool 'latexmk' is installed, build 'doct.tex' using
'latexmk'. Otherwise, compile the document manually using the standard
LaTeX build sequence:

1. Build doct.tex using pdflatex
2. Build doct.bib using bibtex
3. Build doct.tex using pdflatex
4. Build doct.tex using pdflatex

Thank you. 

